How to keep agentic workloads orchestrated, fast and affordable



plan -> build -> secure & govern -> observe & evaluate -> optimize



Optimization is continuous

Agent Problems:
 - agent sprawl
 - no shared memory
 - tool duplication
 - ungoverened identity
 - observability gaps
 - model lock-in
 - data plane chaos
 - no cost visibility


Architecture problem not a model problem


Latency = Loops x (L LLM + L Tool + L Net)

compounding issues 
 - toekn cost grows non-linearly
 - latency erodes trust
 - RAG returns Noise
 - Orchedstration Overhead Multiplies

Agent Systems Anti-Patterns 
 - Monolithic Agent Anti-Pattern
    - one god agent
 - Unbounded loop anti-patern
    - failed retry runs indefinitely
 - Context Corruption Chain
    - agent writes incorrect state to shared memory
 - Tool Call Ambiguity



5 Layer Optimization Model 
1. Model Selection
    - which model does what work
    - right size for task
2. Skill & Context
    - tokens in / out, 
    - compress, cache, structure prompts, histories
3. Retrieval Quality
    - what knowledge reaches model
4. Orechestration
    - how agents / tools coordinate
    - bound loops, parallelize independent work
5. Infrastructure
    - capcity provistioned / routed
    - multi-region deployemnt
    - hybrid capacity


