Choose right mechanism 

Skill for procedures 
    - how do we do x here
RAG for knowledge
    - what is true right now
Tools  for actions
    - do X now
Fine-tuning for behavior 

Agent Complexity Ladder: 

L1:  Single Agent + Bounded Tool Set
L2:  Single Agent + Deterministic Workflow Steps
L3:  Planner Agent + Specialist Sub-Agents
L4:  Peer Multi-Agent Meshhh


Tool Call Optimizaton Patterns: 
 - parallel tool execution
 - result summarization 
 - minimal tool description
 - tool call caching (Redis)

Agent Optimizer  << Foundry Agent Service
1. Evaluate the base line
2. Generate candidates
    - new instructions, skills or models
3. Evaluate candidates
4. Rank and recommend
    - sorted by score, per task breakdowns and token cost
5. Deploy the winnder

clear tool name 
- verb_noun  (get_customer, create_ticket)

collapse into one agent (+ skills)                      split into multiple agents


BOUND EVERY AGENT RUN 
- fail cheap and immediately

- token and cost budget
    - per-run and per-tenant budgets enforced in the orhcestrator
- turn and depth limits
    - hard cap on loops
- timeouts & fallbacks
- tracing built-in


RAG Optimization pipeline

1. Chunking Strategy 
    - 512 - 1024 tokens 
    - semantic chunking beats fixed-size chunking
    - enrich, title, lable

2. Embedding mdoel
    1526-dim for larcge corporation
    768-dim for focusted domain

3. Hybrid Search
4. Semantic Reranking
    - cross encoder re-score top-k candidate
5. Metadata Filtering

Retrieval evals 
 - measure
 - diagnose
 - tune
 - ship and re-measure

Latency is an infrastrucure problem

- Location
- TTFT: Time to First Token
    - shrink context 
    - colocate services
    - stream immediatly
- Inter-token Latency
    - smaller models per step
    - capacity sizing 


Ideal Agentic Loop 
 - hydrate state  (see deck)

Scale, Reliability, Governance (see deck)

Reliability Patterns: 
 - Stateless Rehydration  
    APIM -> compute -> load state from Cosmos DB -> execute -> write back -> free thread
 - Multi-Region Load Balancing
    - round-roben
    - priority-based : PTU primaty +paygo fallback 
    - weighted 70/30

Scaling across regions
- Global 
    - best capacity and price 
    - default for latency teolerant residency flexible workload

- Data ZOne
    - processing constrainted to geographic zone (EU)
- Regional
    - pinned to ....


AI Gateway Patterns
- real-time telemetry & chargeback at token level
- semantic caching powers cost efficiency + performance
- standardized policies
- able to scale to 1000s

Cost Attribution Governance: 
 - Tag spend by workload, team, env
 - APIM token metrics per application, budgets and alerts before month end
 - Report cost per resolved task to stakeholders, not raw token counts
 - APIM rate limiting, per application token budgets

Continuous cost optimization

APIM for AI Workloads
 - cost attribution with every API call w/ worklaod tags, team id
 - per app token quotas



A/B Testing w/ APIM weighted routing 
 - compare quality, latency, cost, failure rate

Canary rollout: 
Awareness, Evaluation, Shador, 5% for 48h, 10%, 25%, 50%, 100%, retire

